{% comment %}
  TRMNL full-screen panel: the daily Hacker News meme. 800x480, 1-bit.

  The picture arrives as a URL, not as data -- a webhook carries 2KB and a meme
  is a few hundred KB -- so memes.storage uploads it to a public bucket and
  TRMNL's renderer fetches it when it draws. It is already dithered to 1-bit by
  memes.eink, so it must not be scaled here: resampling a dithered image
  destroys the dither pattern and turns it to grey mush. Hence the explicit
  width/height and no max-width rule.

  Two layouts, chosen in memes.eink from the template's aspect ratio, because a
  meme carries its own burned-in caption and how far the picture shrinks decides
  whether that caption can be read:

    stack -- wide meme (most of them). Picture fills the panel, headline on one
             footer line. Leaves the meme at roughly 84-97% of original size.
    side  -- square meme (drake). Picture beside a headline column, which is
             what earns back the white space a square would otherwise waste.

  The headline is real text rather than part of the picture, so TRMNL renders it
  at native resolution instead of it being dithered along with the photograph.
{% endcomment %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Barlow+Condensed:wght@600;800&amp;family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;600&amp;display=swap">
<div class="view view--full">
  <div style="width: 800px; height: 480px; box-sizing: border-box; background: #ffffff; color: #000000; display: flex; flex-direction: column; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, 'DejaVu Sans Mono', monospace; -webkit-font-smoothing: none;">

    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; padding: 7px 20px; background: #000000; color: #ffffff; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 2px; flex-shrink: 0;">
      <span>HACKER NEWS &middot; DAILY MEME</span>
      <span>{{ day }}</span>
    </div>

    {% if layout == "stack" %}

      <div style="flex-grow: 1; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; overflow: hidden;">
        <img src="{{ meme_url }}" width="{{ meme_width }}" height="{{ meme_height }}" alt="{{ headline }}" style="display: block; image-rendering: pixelated;">
      </div>
      <div style="flex-shrink: 0; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 16px; padding: 6px 20px; border-top: 3px solid #000000;">
        <span style="font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'IBM Plex Mono', sans-serif; font-weight: 600; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.1; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis;">{{ headline | truncate: 72 }}</span>
        {% if points != blank %}
          <span style="font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 1px; white-space: nowrap;">{{ points }} PTS &middot; {{ comments }} C</span>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

    {% else %}

      <div style="display: flex; flex-grow: 1; align-items: stretch; overflow: hidden;">
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 6px 8px 6px 10px;">
          <img src="{{ meme_url }}" width="{{ meme_width }}" height="{{ meme_height }}" alt="{{ headline }}" style="display: block; image-rendering: pixelated;">
        </div>
        <div style="flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 0; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 14px 18px 12px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #000000; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between;">
          <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;">
            <span style="font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 2px;">FRONT PAGE</span>
            <span style="font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'IBM Plex Mono', sans-serif; font-weight: 600; font-size: 25px; line-height: 1.12;">{{ headline | truncate: 110 }}</span>
          </div>
          {% if points != blank %}
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; border-top: 2px solid #000000; padding-top: 6px; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 1px;">
              <span>{{ points }} POINTS</span>
              <span>{{ comments }} COMMENTS</span>
            </div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>

    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
